WEBVTT

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:17.050
Tell everyone we'll be having
our meeting at the usual time.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.390
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.060
Wow. This really is a village.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.480
Karita, make sure
the gate is locked up tight.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.900
There may be some rats lurking around.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.860
Who are you calling "rats"?

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.530
I think he means you.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:32.440
Hey.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:35.070
Ran, I'll join you
after I check the crop shed.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.160
Got it.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.160
Hey!

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.740
This isn't a parade for you to gawk at.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.040
-Get to work.
-Yes, sir.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.960
I take my eyes off them for a second
and they start slacking off.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.500
AUTUMN BEGINS

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:15.920
Did you build this village?

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:18.970
Yes, Akiwo and I built it.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:22.600
So, where are the other members
of your team?

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.180
In Kyushu.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.390
We found one of the seven
regional Fuji mountains. We're there.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.730
And why did you come all the way here?

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:34.320
To check out the Kanto region
because these two used to live there.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.240
On our way, we just happened to run into
that dude from earlier.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.240
What do you think, Akiwo?

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.870
I don't believe in coincidences.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:47.000
How can we be sure you aren't here
just to steal from us?

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.540
"Steal"?

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.000
Look, we only stopped here because
we heard one of the Fujis was in Kobe.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:53.500
This is it.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:54.880
For real?

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.380
Mt. Futatabi, also known as Mt. Kobe Fuji.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.630
This house was built right on top
of the storage shelter.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.350
You all got some really clean clothes on.
When did you wake up in this world?

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:07.060
About a month ago.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:09.310
So, that's how it is.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.560
So it's different for each team, then.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.570
We've already been here for three years.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:16.570
Three years?

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.150
Didn't you meet anyone else
during that time?

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:24.070
We spent a year wandering,
then another year making our home here.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:28.790
Now in the third year, you all are
the first people we've come across.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.290
But I'm disappointed.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:31.960
What's that supposed to mean?

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.380
Time for the meeting.

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:40.050
Sakuya, what did you accomplish today?

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:44.970
I harvested the corn
and took care of the livestock as usual.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.810
I also cleaned the shed.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:47.930
Understood.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:49.640
Karita, you're next.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:53.940
I cultivated a new field on the west slope
and spread earthworms.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.690
-I'm going to leave for a while.
-I see.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.150
-Where are you going?
-Next, Akane.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:00.110
Nature calls.
You want to come with me, Nat?

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.280
No, I'm fine.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.660
Okay, save my seat.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.450
Where is Semimaru going?

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.450
The bathroom.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.710
-Kurumi.
-Yes, ma'am.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:12.960
That was all you could manage?

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:17.210
I'm sorry. My hands hurt,
so I couldn't make much progress.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.750
You've been slacking off.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.260
You decided your own quota, didn't you?

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.970
I'm sorry. I'll make up for it tomorrow.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:30.220
Please stop!
I'll help her make up for it. Just stop.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.930
You can barely even handle your own quota.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.400
Don't pretend like you can play the hero.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.230
That's enough!

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.320
What the hell is this
supposed to accomplish?

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.860
Ryuusei, in addition to cutting wood,
I'm putting you on bath duty tonight.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.990
You'll also do the night patrol.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.330
Aren't you the guide of this group?

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.290
Don't just watch. Please stop this.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:55.960
Hey...

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.840
It doesn't matter
what you say to that man.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:02.090
Izayoi is as weak and indecisive
as his name sounds.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.840
He was the only adult.
He knew what he was getting into,

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.720
but he ran away from the responsibility.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:11.850
I'm sorry.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:16.100
He only wears those glasses
to hide his face and avoid reality.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:17.940
Isn't that right, Mr. Guide?

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.360
Start over when you gather the courage
to take off those glasses.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:24.860
But I doubt that day will ever come.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.660
Who died and made you two kings?

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.570
We were forced into this mess together!

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.740
We have to cooperate!

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.500
And why aren't you speaking up?

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.540
It's stupid to let them beat you!

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.210
Wake up!

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.710
We all came here as equals, didn't we?

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.670
Listen, boy.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:45.970
Not all people are equal.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.300
That hurts.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.640
-Let me go.
-This man,

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.430
he was trying to steal food from us.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:55.980
-That hurt.
-Semimaru.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.480
They're thieves, just like I thought.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.480
Well, I was just hoping for some charity.

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:03.980
The punishment is severe, pal.

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:08.860
Hold up! I take it back.
It was just a joke! A prank!

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:12.080
People with sticky fingers get punished.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.080
No way!

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.120
Wait a minute! All we want to do is
get to the Kanto region.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.120
Naturally, we would be happy
if you shared with us,

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:20.670
but we have no intention of stealing.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:22.590
Share with you?

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:24.750
In exchange for what, exactly?

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:25.670
What?

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.130
There is no money in this world.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:31.430
What are you going to give us, pretty boy?

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:37.810
Just so you know,
you won't make it to the Kanto region.

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:42.690
Even if you somehow did,
I doubt you would make it back alive.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:44.690
What are you talking about?

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.320
It's physically impossible.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.450
Hey, Karita.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.700
Tie up this bunch of thieves.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:52.570
What the heck are you doing?

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:54.120
-Just try and catch me
-Yes, sir.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.450
-if you--
-Hey! Stop!

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:58.460
-Don't even bother trying to resist.
-Damn it.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:01.040
-Karita is an Olympic level judo athlete.
-Let go!

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:06.460
Wait. If you're so strong,
why are you letting them push you around?

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:09.800
I think you've got
the wrong idea about us.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:13.970
The whole reason we're still alive is
thanks to Mr. Akiwo and Ms. Ran.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:18.560
It's true that not all people are equal.

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:22.480
Some people have the strength to live,
and some don't.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:23.480
What?

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:24.770
Are you serious?

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:28.740
Those two are the ones
who whip the rest of us into shape.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:31.490
So would you please just drop it?

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.890
Why are you speaking in English?

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.940
Use it or lose it, as they say.

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:08.780
What are you all supposed to be good at?

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:11.030
We all have some special skill.

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:13.150
It's the reason we got chosen.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:17.120
From what I can tell,
the pretty boy is probably an athlete.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:21.000
And the other one is nothing more than
a habitual shoplifter, I guess?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.290
Hey, have some respect.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.500
And what about you, girlie?

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.420
What? Me?

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:30.340
Oh, nothing.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:31.630
"Nothing"?

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:33.470
No skills or knowledge?

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:34.720
Nothing.

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:40.560
Didn't that coward of a guide mention
that there are two Summer teams?

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:41.520
Yes.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.350
So which are you?

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:44.890
Team B.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:49.320
They're the dropouts.
That would explain the shoplifter.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:55.700
How ludicrous. Even talking to them
was a waste of time.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:56.700
How can you say that?

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.160
What the hell is your problem?

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.290
You may be pretty,
but don't let it go to your head.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:01.450
Oh, jeez.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:05.210
Hey, boy. You want to know something?

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:08.290
What's that?

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:10.880
Having sex is banned in our team.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.380
Can you figure out why?

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:18.390
Because they didn't leave us
any contraceptives.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:21.560
We're not going to pump out babies
like they want us to.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:23.930
Japan can rot for all I care!

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:28.440
Hey! Wait! Get back here!

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:30.400
What are you going to do with us?

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:33.400
Untie this rope right now! Goddamn it!

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:39.370
Damn, it's not coming loose.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.170
That sure sucked.

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:48.370
That was dangerous.

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.000
Are you all right?

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.800
More or less.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:53.920
You...

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:55.340
Oh, don't worry.

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:57.340
Nobody has noticed.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.470
Have some water.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:00.890
Here.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:03.260
Thank you.

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.020
Hold on a second.

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:15.820
You know, I'm not a trusting person
like you two are.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:17.740
In other words...

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.950
It's in my nature to suspect everyone.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.210
Poison?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.630
Just look!
That dude has clearly lost his marbles!

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:33.800
Stop right there.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.710
Mr. Izayoi, what are you doing?

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:37.920
Isn't this everyone's drinking water?

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:39.590
Are you trying to kill them all?

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:41.220
Why would you do this?

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:43.560
We're better off dead.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.720
We should all just die.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:49.890
Why? Why are we still alive?

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:53.980
I should have done this sooner.

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:56.780
This was given to all of the guides,

00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:00.410
a cyanide compound that can kill everyone

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:05.240
if we woke up
in a world that was uninhabitable.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:07.750
Or if we contracted a disease
that didn't kill,

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.790
but made life impossible,

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.420
this would end it all without suffering.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:13.710
You dumb--

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:15.130
You dumbass!

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.720
What gives you the right?

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:25.600
You think you already know everything
about this world?

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:28.310
I haven't given up yet.

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:29.810
Don't you dare kill me!

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:32.270
Don't kill anyone, you dumbass!

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.540
Now you won't be tempted to use it.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.330
We're going to survive.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:52.960
That's right! So don't get in our way.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:02.970
Those three hit the road.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.800
Good. They should get a taste of
what real despair is like.

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:14.600
If they think they'll be happy after that,
then I would like to see them try.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:22.490
Through all the ages, we've never known
what the meaning of life is.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:24.200
That poison...

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:26.490
Ms. Botan must have a vial of it, right?

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:28.330
Yes, probably.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:30.790
I wonder if she considered using it?

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:31.830
I doubt that.

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:33.790
That woman is not the type.

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:35.830
Yes, you're right.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:40.590
Why is there an ocean here?

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:42.550
This should be the right direction.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:46.180
Let's get the boat set up.
We'll just have to keep going.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:50.470
Hey, there isn't anywhere to tie it down.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:52.180
Oh, is that so?

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:56.230
Someone will have to stay behind
to hold it.

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:58.610
Then how are they supposed to get down?

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:01.110
There's no way I'm jumping into
that ocean full of rocks.

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:03.490
-Do you want to stay here, then?
-What?

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:05.030
Are you trying to leave me behind?

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:07.410
No thanks! If someone has to stay,
then you should do it.

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:10.240
I sure as hell don't want to
go back to that village.

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:14.710
I'll help lower you all down.

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:16.920
Mr. Izayoi.

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:19.000
You followed us?

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:22.840
There's no way in hell we can trust you.
You would just let the rope go.

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:25.840
I want you to go east and check it out.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:29.930
If you find anything good out there,

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.770
I want you to return and tell Team Autumn.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:34.890
Please.

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:40.650
What do you think?

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:44.190
Mr. Izayoi, if you don't mind,

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:46.240
will you take off your glasses for us?

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:51.410
I find it hard to trust those
who intentionally hide their eyes.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.910
Sure, I can understand that.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:00.920
I should have done this from the start.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:04.420
Hey, you're good-looking!
Those glasses don't do you any favors.

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:10.890
<i>I used to make a living as a firefighter.</i>

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:13.470
<i>I've always wanted to help people.</i>

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:16.850
<i>I thought I was ready for all this,</i>

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:18.270
<i>but somewhere in my heart,</i>

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:22.270
<i>I guess I never truly believed
things would end up like this.</i>

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:26.280
<i>We can always make up for our mistakes
as long as we're alive.</i>

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:29.070
<i>You've already survived
for three years, right?</i>

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:30.660
<i>You'll make it.</i>

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:36.250
<i>Please find a way to maintain
that optimism of yours.</i>

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:41.170
<i>Do whatever it takes
to keep your hope alive.</i>

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:52.470
Hey! That's land over there, right?

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:53.680
Yes.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:56.520
Looks like eastern Japan is still intact.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:02.060
I take back what I said.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:10.070
We've come a long way from Kobe.

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:14.330
I get the feeling we passed Hamamatsu
without even knowing it.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:18.580
Wait, didn't you say
that's where you used to live?

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:19.830
Yes.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:23.210
Apparently, there's nothing left
of Hamamatsu anymore.

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:26.960
That probably means the eels
it was famous for are now extinct, too.

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:31.630
Well, my family could never
afford to eat them, anyway.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:36.310
Guess that's it.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:38.430
Time to say my goodbyes.

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:41.640
<i>Hey, Mom.</i>

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.310
<i>You were unlucky in love,</i>

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:47.320
<i>but with your devil's luck,
you may be alive somewhere.</i>

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:52.070
<i>That 100 million yen you got
for selling me, what did you spend it on?</i>

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:54.070
<i>Men?</i>

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:56.450
<i>I bet you did, Mom.</i>

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:58.410
Isn't this...

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.040
There's an entrance just like the others.

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:03.830
Heave-ho!

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.380
-It won't budge. Hey!
-This is another one of the seven.

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:08.800
-Help me out here.
-Mt. Ogino Fuji.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:10.670
-I can't do this by myself.
-Or Mt. Kyogatake.

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:12.340
If that's right,

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:15.050
then we're already in Kanagawa prefecture.

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:19.140
But I didn't see Mt. Fuji anywhere.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:22.140
It's been totally flooded.

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:24.060
Maybe it's groundwater.

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:26.520
It's drinkable
if we filter and boil it, right?

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:28.400
I'm going to dive in and take a look.

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:32.200
Hold up, Arashi! You have no idea
if there's a way for you to get out.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:33.240
Don't do it!

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:34.740
Arashi...

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:41.200
It seems like he's getting more desperate
the closer we get to Tokyo.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:55.720
<i>Hana...</i>

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:19.200
Please don't be dead.

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:21.990
Please be alive somewhere...

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.210
Hana.

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:29.090
We'll stay here tonight.

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:31.210
Once we have enough supplies,
we'll head for Tokyo.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:34.840
All right, time to start a fire.

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:36.970
Hey, fire wiz, use this.

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:41.600
Wait, isn't this from your book?
Are you sure?

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:42.640
It's fine.

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:43.560
<i>ROBINSON CRUSOE</i>

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:45.020
It's only half of the book, anyway.

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:46.640
<i>Hana...</i>

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:51.650
The greenery here is thick
and the air is heavy.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:53.900
It's hard to breathe.

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:55.860
Maybe there's too much oxygen.

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:58.780
It's quiet.

00:17:58.860 --> 00:17:59.990
"Quiet"?

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:02.450
I hear a lot of different noises
around here.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:04.790
At least, compared to the last island.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:11.460
Hey! Somebody!

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:14.880
Is anybody out there?

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:21.890
No matter what happened, don't you think
some people had a chance to flee?

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:23.810
Just look at how many buildings are left.

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:25.980
It's impossible to say.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:29.730
What? You want me to make you feel better?

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:33.520
What's your problem?
Isn't there someone you're worried about?

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:37.610
Isn't there someone special to you,
someone you want to be alive?

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:41.030
No, there isn't.

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:42.490
What?

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:44.910
Actually, this is all a big relief for me.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:48.620
Everyone we knew isn't alive anymore.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:52.750
And without them, music will die out too.

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.550
My family has practiced music
for generations.

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:59.260
Their children all had to play
the piano or violin.

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:02.090
It was stressful and scary.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:05.260
There was never even a chance...

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:08.850
to enjoy the sounds.

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:12.270
You didn't enjoy it at all?

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.610
No, and now I never have to play
the piano again.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:19.650
I've never felt so free.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.700
I think we can get in here.

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:31.920
Let's spend the night inside
and then hurry back tomorrow.

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:33.670
Sounds good to me.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.880
I'm tired of rowing. It ruins my hands.

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:43.260
A church?

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:46.060
Isn't it just a chapel for weddings?

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:48.270
Haru?

00:19:58.190 --> 00:19:59.320
Want to try?

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:02.030
I'll pass.
I don't want to injure my fingers.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:08.700
So tell me, who is this person
you want to meet so badly?

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:10.080
A boyfriend?

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:13.040
Yes, his name is Arashi.

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:18.420
You know,

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:22.430
sometimes Olympic athletes
get a lot of flak

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:24.890
for saying that they enjoyed the race.

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:30.140
But that totally doesn't mean
they aren't serious or are taking it easy.

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:33.390
I imagine that they enjoy
the thrill they feel

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:39.650
while under the extreme stress
and intensity of the competition.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:42.700
What? What are you talking about?

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:48.280
I think athletes and artists know best
what that moment of happiness is like.

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:50.330
Wasn't it the same for you, Haru?

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:52.750
It must have been.

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:55.250
If you really don't want to play
the piano anymore,

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:58.590
then why are you always wearing gloves
and protecting your hands?

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:09.350
Haru?

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:45.650
<i>Haru, I can see the road
that you've traveled.</i>

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:04.800
Fujiko and the others are back!

00:23:05.380 --> 00:23:06.260
Fujiko.

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:09.340
Hey, Fujiko! How did it go?

00:23:09.840 --> 00:23:12.340
It's just ocean
all the way to Mt. Tsukuba.

00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:15.560
The plains of Kanto are
totally underwater.

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:17.270
I see.

00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:18.640
Hey!

00:23:21.020 --> 00:23:22.150
Hey!

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:25.270
If Tokyo is no more,

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:28.490
then our only option
is to head for Mt. Fuji.

00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:30.700
You're right.

00:23:30.780 --> 00:23:33.280
Haru, what was that song
you played earlier?

00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:34.990
"Morning Mood" from <i>Peer Gynt</i>.

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:37.620
I thought it was pretty fitting
for us right now.

00:23:38.120 --> 00:23:41.120
It was amazing. It made me cry.

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:44.290
You're exaggerating.
That organ didn't even work.

00:23:44.380 --> 00:23:47.000
Still, it made me feel better.

00:23:48.300 --> 00:23:50.840
Well, it wasn't too bad of a performance,

00:23:51.880 --> 00:23:53.220
if I do say so myself.

00:23:53.300 --> 00:23:57.560
Yes. As long as you're still alive,
music will never die out.
